        "en": "But no one can fail to profit from M. Marcel's work, provided he takes it seriously, provided, that is, he doesn't go to him as a ^eading.Christian existentialist' whom he must read in order to* be in the mode! M. Marcel deprecates the label, preferring to call himself 'a concrete philosopher' that is a philosopher who is not prepared to sacrifice to the demands of systematic natures sensitivity to the rough edges of human life."
