        "en": "3. The book should be widely read by the many Christian 'fellow-travellers' of today, those who follow, as it were, afar off the Christian way without themselves coming yet to the point of an act of faith in the Crucified. Its very incompleteness will respond to their groping anxiety, and it will enrich their vision of life. And this it can do because it eschews dogmatic exposition seeking rather to shew the inside of the truly Christian way of life. Fidelity, hope, chirity, mystery these are fundamental categories of the Christian way: and of all these Marcel has much to say, which is in every way fresh and yet at the same time rootedjnjhe tradition of Catholic Christianity."
