        "en": "We have here, I think, the elements of a criterion for judging whether the belief in immortality has any religious value in it or not: the whole question is whether it looks like an act of faith and love, or like an arrogation rooted in the concern for self. (Note written August, 1934.) On the other hand, its possible loss is, as it were, the reverse side or disastrous counterpart of all possession."
