        "fr": "piétons qu’on emprunte lorsqu'une voie est barrée et qui débouche sur cette voie au-delà de l’obstacle.",
        "en": "And yet, in all this I find something unsatisfactory; and I still cannot manage to formulate it in my own mind. I do see clearly, however, that I am in complete opposition to such attitudes as Griscbach's; I see in memory one essential aspect of the ontological assertion. How much nearer I feel to Bergson in this regard, and also to St. Augustine! What is witness in Bergson? surely a consecration. But the very notion of consecration is an ambiguous one, and we must beware of interpreting it in a pragmatist sense."
