        "en": "November 22nd. — I was talking to the abbe A yesterday about Theresa Neumann. This morning I was thinking with exasperation of the rationalist's attitude to such facts. They would refuse to give them a hearing. Reflecting next upon my own exasperation, I thought it 1 Appendix of the Journal Mttapbysique. (Ed. N.R.F.) 2 A possible way towards a theory of eucharistic presence. (Note written October 10th, 1934.) ill was surely to be traced to some residue of doubt in myself. If I were absolutely sure, I should only experience a feeling of pure charity and pity for doubters. I think this discovery is far-reaching. It seems to me that charity is bound up with being sure. This must be developed. 1"
