        "en": "We must look more closely into my remarks on intuition; for it is not yet perfectly clear to me. I am really talking about an intuition which is, as it were, active and purely active an intuition, in fact, of which I could not in any manner have the disposal. But its presence is expressed by the ontological unease which is at work in reflection. To explain this we should start with an example or illustration; perhaps the demand for purity or even for truth. This intuition is not in me. There is something to be discovered or invented here, if one does not wish to remain in a state of negation."
