        "fr": "plus Exactement il n’est rien de ce qui peut s’énoncer que l’un de nous ne puisse à un moment donné croire, penser. Les facilités du langage de tous points comparables à celles que dispense un réseau de communications extrémement perfectionnées. Mais en soi circuler n’est rien — et discourir n’est. rien, est moins encore. Ces remarques m'étaient suggérées par je ne sais plus quelle pseudo- appréciation esthétique, mais hélas ! elles trouveraient aussi leur application dans tant de pseudo-métaphysiques.",
        "en": "Bring this to bear on the very notion of truth. Shew the postulate or hidden method of representation which is taken for granted by those who think that the mind must be autonomous in its pursuit of the truth. This is still not absolutely clear to me today. It seems to me that we always start from a twofold notion, of a field to be developed, and also of an equipment which will make this development possible. It is as though we would not let ourselves admit that this equipment can be supplemented a\\\\\\\\> extra. We say that it would no be cheating; we add that it would anyhow be impossible really to bring it off."
