        "en": "We must not overlook the fact that all spiritual possession has its brought to light the sort of dialectic in virtue of which the philosopher is led to deny himself as a 'Fachmcnsch', as a specialist. (Note written September, 1934.) springs in something that cannot be shewn (my ideas are rooted in what I am). But what characterises this non-she wable as such, is the fact that it does not belong to me, it is essentially uribelonging. There is therefore a sense in which I do not belong to myself, and this is exactly the sense in which I am absolutely not autonomous."
