        "en": "In so far as I conceive myself as having in myself, or more exactly, as mine, certain characteristics, certain trappings, I consider myself from the point of view of another but I do not separate myself from this other except after having first implicitly identified myself with him. When I say, for instance, 'I have my own opinion about that,' I imply, 'My opinion is not everybody's*; but I can only exclude or reject everybody's opinion if I have first, by a momentary fiction, assimilated it and made it mine."
