        "en": "It is plain that its corollary, 'Pride is a source of blindness', is an essential pan of the 'library of human wisdom*. It is one of those truisms that lie buried under the dust of ages, and no one troubles to dig them up again because everyone thinks that their spiritual fertility is for ever exhausted. And yet, if we did take the trouble to apply this commonplace of personal ethics to the realm of depersonalised thought (so-called), we might be astonished to see what unexpected horizons unfolded before our eyes."
